div.p:
1. To accept the principle of the establishment of a scenario, the first stages
                    of which would be defined precisely, and the subsequent stages would be defined
                    in detail as events evolve;

quote.p:
(2) express understanding and regret for the grievances of the Iranian
                        people, including the widespread perception of U.S. intervention in Iran’s
                        internal affairs;

note.p:
Source: Carter Library, National Security Affairs, Brzezinski Material, Country File, Box 31, Iran 2/80. Secret;
                    Nodis; Cherokee; Flash. An unknown hand
                    wrote “advance copy” in the upper right corner. Carter initialed “C” in the upper right corner.
